  "methodologyRevision": "V8 proved that constructing 512 ComparatorLoad values and blocking shared response delivery was not sufficient: Fovea makeLoad returned after creating an events stream, while its internal pipeline task could reach the exact fetch registry later. A clean V8 repeat still created a seventeenth shared origin request with only eight origin gate waiters. V9 adds an explicit ComparatorLoad.waitUntilPrepared contract. W7 awaits all 512 preparation operations before releasing /w7/shared responses. Fovea preparation proves ordinal 1...32 exact fetch subscriber registration per shared identity; adapters that install native operations asynchronously signal only after their task, receipt or UUID is installed. Synchronous adapters use makeLoad return as the preparation boundary. Response-delivery gating, cancellation, priority, service budgets, endpoints and statistics are otherwise unchanged.",
